	(text_box "SENSE PATH -- CS -> R_SNS -> 4.7 k -> SNS_x, CLAMPED ON THE ADC SIDE ONLY (Review Focus 4)\nR68-R70 = 1.8 kOhm set the scale: 3.0 V at the 0.5 A limit (K = 300), 0.48 V at 80 mA.\nOn a short or over-temperature the CS pin goes to its 4.5-6.5 V fault level.  R71-R73 (4.7 kOhm)\nthen carry (6.5 - 3.3 - 0.3) / 4.7 k = 0.6 mA into the BAT54 (D8-D10, anode SNS_x, cathode\n+3V3_ALW), which holds the ADC pin at ~3.6 V.  The clamp sits on SNS_x deliberately: on the CS\nnode it would have no series resistor to limit its current.\nC44-C46 (10 nF) at the ADC end supply the SAR sample-and-hold charge locally; tau with 4.7 k is 47 us, so firmware settles >= 250 us\nafter changing DIAG_SEL before reading.  A reading above ~3.0 V means fault, not current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 65.48 0)
		(size 103.19 13.84)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e1fd7e8-fb7f-5ccb-befa-86799d765640")
	)
	(text_box "CURRENT LIMIT, THERMAL MODE, FAULT, GROUND\nCL: R62-R64 = 4.02 kOhm -> 0.8 V x 2500 / 4.02 k = 0.50 A per channel (Eq. 4).\nTHER: R65-R67 = 10 kOhm to the GATED +5V -> latch-off while awake, so the firmware owns retry with\nbackoff (spec 6.3); with +5V off in sleep the pin's internal pull-down draws nothing.\nFAULT: not connected -- no GPIO left; the per-chip sense line reports faults (4.5-6.5 V level).\nGND pads and the exposed pad go straight to GND: feed A's LTC4380 already blocks reverse\npolarity, so TI's GND resistor/diode network is not fitted."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 51.62 0)
		(size 103.19 12.36)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5f0b530b-7201-5d81-b549-678f201fa7c3")
	)
	(text_box "INPUTS -- WHY EVERY IN NET IS LOW AT RESET\nEach OUT_* GPIO reaches its IN pin through R_IN_SERIES (4.7 kOhm, TI 7.3.7.5) and the IN net\ncarries R_IN_PULLDOWN (47 kOhm) to GND, so no channel can light while the ESP32 is in reset, in\ndownload mode or asleep.  Driven high: 3.3 V x 37.0 k / (37.0 k + 4.7 k) = 2.93 V against\nVIH = 2.0 V (47 k in parallel with the 175 k minimum internal pull-down).  Series R40-R49,\npull-downs R50-R61.\nDIAG_EN_Q, DIAG_SEL0_Q and DIAG_SEL1_Q are shared by all three chips.  Their 4.7 kOhm series resistors and the 10 kOhm DIAG_EN_Q pull-\ndown live on mcu_can; SEL0/SEL1 have no external pull (their level is irrelevant while DIAG_EN is low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 36.28 0)
		(size 103.19 13.84)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6030b66c-fad0-5417-a12a-cd96a944b260")
	)
	(text_box "AUX OUTPUTS -- PLACEHOLDERS ONLY (spec 9.1, kit-gated)\nOUT_AUX_L and OUT_AUX_R each end in one 47 kOhm pull-down (R74, R75) and nothing else.  The\nswitch stage, the pod tail and the R100 re-size are kit-gated (spec 9.1) and are added in the\nkit plan, not here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 80.82 0)
		(size 103.19 7.92)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "77a8c267-7574-5d0d-8700-a156b9733cc6")
	)
	(text_box "U13 CH3 -- RESERVED FOR AUX_MODE (spec 3), WIRED IN THE KIT PLAN.  U13 CH4 -- SPARE.\nBoth spare inputs are pulled down (R60, R61) and both spare outputs are no-connect.  Do not\nre-use U13 ch3 for anything else: the kit plan needs it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 28.34 0)
		(size 103.19 6.44)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7d5228f5-cd6f-5a6f-948d-0611a228354b")
	)
	(text_box "SIGNAL OUTPUTS (spec 4.4, plan4 decision D1) -- three TI TPS4H160B-Q1 quads, ten channels, two spare\n         CH1        CH2        CH3        CH4        sense\n  U11    FL_DRL     FL_IND     RL_DRL     RL_IND     SNS_A   (left)\n  U12    FR_DRL     FR_IND     RR_DRL     RR_IND     SNS_B   (right)\n  U13    RL_BRK     RR_BRK     spare      spare      SNS_C   (brake)\nOne dead chip never takes out both sides' indicators, and brake survives a side chip failing. Both OUT pads of each channel are tied to\nthe channel's net.  No output capacitor: TI's typical application (Fig. 8-1) shows none.  VS is VBAT (feed A, behind the LTC4380) with\none 100 nF 100 V 0805 per chip (C41-C43) -- the SMBJ24A clamps at 50.6 V, so nothing on VBAT is under 63 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 13 0)
		(size 103.19 13.84)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8af0977f-9011-5cf2-b316-73541fab9d1f")
	)
	(text_box "HARNESS TAILS (D5) -- SOLDERED WIRE, NOT CONNECTORS\nJ3 front: FL_DRL, FL_IND, FR_DRL, FR_IND, GND.  J4 rear part 1: RL_DRL, RL_IND, RL_BRK, GND.\nJ5 rear part 2: RR_DRL, RR_IND, RR_BRK.  J8: CAN twisted pair.\nJ4 and J5 are one 7-core cable through one gland, split across two tails only because KiCad's Connector_Wire relief footprints stop at\n1x06; the 7-core run has one return (spec 3.1), on J4. The Superseal joints sit out on the harness.  The _Relief footprints' second,\nunplated hole per conductor is the strain relief: nothing else mechanically restrains these wires."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 460.0 90.24 0)
		(size 103.19 10.88)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f868b0a7-d5dd-5ce8-8f29-0afb34311e32")
	)
